WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.497
EXTRACT reads one component from a date or timestamp.

00:00:03.497 --> 00:00:09.687
You can extract year, month, day of week, hour, and many other fields.

00:00:09.687 --> 00:00:14.297
The result is a component value, not a new grouped timestamp.

00:00:14.297 --> 00:00:18.792
This distinction matters when comparing EXTRACT with DATE_TRUNC.

00:00:18.792 --> 00:00:27.477
EXTRACT returns a component such as month number or year; DATE_TRUNC returns a timestamp aligned to a time

00:00:27.477 --> 00:00:29.372
boundary such as the start of the month.

00:00:29.372 --> 00:00:35.972
For grouping over multiple years, truncating to month is often safer than grouping by month number alone

00:00:35.972 --> 00:00:42.207
because January 2025 and January 2026 should not be merged accidentally.
